  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Mariagenspiel (Mariage). Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Mariagenspiel is the historical ancestor of the vast 'Marriage' family of card games, which includes global hits like Sixty-Six, Schnapsen, Pinochle, and Belote. Its name literally means 'Marriage Game', referring to the core mechanic: earning bonus points by holding and declaring a King and Queen of the same suit. It is a trick-taking game where players must balance the pursuit of card points with the opportunistic timing of their marriages.",
    objective: 'Be the first to reach a target score (usually 66 or 100 points) through tricks and marriages.',
    gameplay: '1. **Phase 1**: Players play tricks and then draw a card to stay at 6. No obligation to follow suit.\n2. **Phase 2**: Once the stock is empty, suit-following and trumping rules apply.\n3. **Victory**: A player can declare a marriage only after winning their first trick.',
    keyRules: [
      'Phase 1: no obligation to follow suit; after each trick both players draw to refill to 6.',
      'Phase 2 (stock empty): must follow suit or trump if unable; no more draws or marriage declarations.',
      'Marriage (K+Q same suit): 20 pts plain, 40 in trumps; declare only after winning a trick.',
      '66 card points win the deal; last trick worth 10 extra. Trump 7 may rob the turn-up.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Two players. The game is played by two people; each receives six cards at the start. One card is turned face-up for trump (the seven of trumps may be exchanged for it). While the stock lasts, after each trick both players draw to refill to six cards.',
      deck: '32 cards: Ace, 10, King, Queen, Jack, 9, 8, 7.',
      equipment: '32 cards: Ace, 10, King, Queen, Jack, 9, 8, 7.',
      dealing: 'Each player receives 6 cards. One card is flipped to determine the Trump suit.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. **Phase 1**: Players play tricks and then draw a card to stay at 6. No obligation to follow suit.\n2. **Phase 2**: Once the stock is empty, suit-following and trumping rules apply.\n3. **Victory**: A player can declare a marriage only after winning their first trick.',
